{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3f9a6bce0346428987b51aad7688ebbc8a095abb4f8e9692e697b477a6012454"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repo follows the Agent Skills specification and can be installed via Vercel add-skill, OpenSkills, or Skillset, and is advertised as working with Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Windsurf, Amp, and OpenCode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5cfef2c437f4a1984835c7ec3cc3c7e6664fe1f52cda09c69bc12793a4fdb842"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool runs an iterative loop: each iteration orients from specs, picks one task, implements and tests it, verifies criteria, commits and pushes, then repeats until a DONE marker appears."},{"claim_ids":["clm_60a4e65bc90653f61abc493742e4517f8465be9bd87d52a3ddd3f360cee4a86b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README warns the tool grants AI agents significant autonomy over the codebase and system, advising users to review all changes and run in isolated environments when possible."},{"claim_ids":["clm_679b873b4faed71c7713b5ca64686ecf1c1612b3ff32e459e6d0e8dbce97fccf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Build mode can take an iteration-count argument, e.g. ralph-loop.sh 20 for a maximum of 20 iterations, or run unlimited by default."},{"claim_ids":["clm_806b0ce8ea54bd68c16e2646dd8bd37bfe7fdde8ae2614d55fc88ae69a2f6f65"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"State persists on disk between loops: IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md is read to pick tasks and updated with progress, while each iteration starts with a fresh context window."},{"claim_ids":["clm_92e51fa9f1505abca14ac91957c2d6af977a6a7b04997b81dc7cacca8a86cd97"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each spec tracks an attempt count as an NR_OF_TRIES comment; after 10 attempts without completion a spec is flagged as stuck and should be split into smaller specs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ba1df09cb4c97ce73f242c6f0d3831f8fd2238a929e80e0972de2c9b79a238f1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Completion is gated on a magic phrase: the agent outputs <promise>DONE</promise> only when acceptance criteria are verified, tests pass, and changes are committed and pushed; the loop retries otherwise."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c8dae0f491917aabb4b0b0f8b0ad0550810fe64a1742919014dae28be3df35d1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product is driven by shell scripts: ralph-loop.sh (default build mode) and an optional 'plan' mode invoked as ralph-loop.sh plan, with matching PowerShell .ps1 variants."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d6ca370b2b0720d4b47dda5815e42bf09a64bc6c8ef1b11e068f53d53099e626"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Specs are expected to carry specific, testable acceptance criteria, and tests, lints, and builds act as backpressure that the agent must satisfy before signaling completion."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f8d1071f814782656569037bd4722f66f8ef289e741e6686ff5e94f5250d4287"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A constitution file at .specify/memory/constitution.md is described as the single source of truth for agent behavior, with optional features configured there rather than in scripts."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3f9a6bce0346428987b51aad7688ebbc8a095abb4f8e9692e697b477a6012454","clm_5cfef2c437f4a1984835c7ec3cc3c7e6664fe1f52cda09c69bc12793a4fdb842","clm_60a4e65bc90653f61abc493742e4517f8465be9bd87d52a3ddd3f360cee4a86b","clm_679b873b4faed71c7713b5ca64686ecf1c1612b3ff32e459e6d0e8dbce97fccf","clm_806b0ce8ea54bd68c16e2646dd8bd37bfe7fdde8ae2614d55fc88ae69a2f6f65","clm_92e51fa9f1505abca14ac91957c2d6af977a6a7b04997b81dc7cacca8a86cd97","clm_ba1df09cb4c97ce73f242c6f0d3831f8fd2238a929e80e0972de2c9b79a238f1","clm_c8dae0f491917aabb4b0b0f8b0ad0550810fe64a1742919014dae28be3df35d1","clm_d6ca370b2b0720d4b47dda5815e42bf09a64bc6c8ef1b11e068f53d53099e626","clm_f8d1071f814782656569037bd4722f66f8ef289e741e6686ff5e94f5250d4287"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:01:14Z","created_by_operation":"op_080d0373aeeb484ca70e1e17007108e7","id":"pg_06b096595f6551c59fef936d3f87b11b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/fstandhartinger-ralph-wiggum-readme-md-3f15f0fb83b8-93